# ::ILANG
# ::ROLE{Publish only the reviewed Vultr article and its timestamped evidence; no existing route edits.}
from pathlib import Path

def publish_vultr_article(output):
    target = Path(output) / 'pricing' / 'vultr'
    target.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (target / 'index.html').write_text(ARTICLE, encoding='utf-8')
    (target / 'page.css').write_text(STYLES, encoding='utf-8')
    (target / 'sources.json').write_text(SOURCES, encoding='utf-8')
    return ('/pricing/vultr/', '2026-11-12T08:49:03+00:00')

ARTICLE = '<!doctype html><html lang="en-US"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Vultr pricing: API rates, regional prices and backups | VPS Cost Lens</title><meta name="description" content="Selected Vultr Cloud Compute rates with field-level API sources, separate regional prices and reproducible backup estimates."><link rel="canonical" href="https://vpscostlens.com/pricing/vultr/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./page.css"></head><body><header><a href="/">VPS Cost Lens</a><span>Official-source price index</span></header><main><h1>vultr pricing</h1>\n<p>Vultr&#x27;s <code>vc2-1c-1gb</code> lists a default price of <strong>$5.00/month</strong> [P2.monthly_cost] or <strong>$0.007/hour</strong> [P2.hourly_cost], with <strong>1024 GB</strong> of plan bandwidth [P2.bandwidth]. Its <code>sao</code> regional price is <strong>$7.50/month</strong> [P2.location_cost.sao.monthly_cost]. With Automatic Backups enabled, the corresponding monthly base-plus-backup estimates are <strong>$6.00</strong> and <strong>$9.00</strong> respectively [default or regional monthly × (1 + B)]. These are selected Cloud Compute catalog rates, not a claim about Vultr&#x27;s cheapest product or a final invoice.</p>\n<h2>Selected Cloud Compute plans</h2>\n<p>All amounts are USD. Default prices remain separate from regional overrides. Backup amounts are calculated estimates for an eligible instance with Automatic Backups enabled; they are not additional API price fields.</p>\n<div class="table-wrap"><table>\n<tr><th>Plan</th><th>Default monthly</th><th>Default hourly</th><th>Plan bandwidth</th><th>Backup addition on default monthly base</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>vc2-1c-0.5gb</code> [P1.id]</td><td>$3.50 [P1.monthly_cost]</td><td>$0.005 [P1.hourly_cost]</td><td>512 GB [P1.bandwidth]</td><td>$0.70/month, estimate [P1.monthly_cost × B]</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>vc2-1c-1gb</code> [P2.id]</td><td>$5.00 [P2.monthly_cost]</td><td>$0.007 [P2.hourly_cost]</td><td>1024 GB [P2.bandwidth]</td><td>$1.00/month, estimate [P2.monthly_cost × B]</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>vc2-1c-2gb</code> [P3.id]</td><td>$10.00 [P3.monthly_cost]</td><td>$0.014 [P3.hourly_cost]</td><td>2048 GB [P3.bandwidth]</td><td>$2.00/month, estimate [P3.monthly_cost × B]</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>数据取自 Vultr 官方接口 · 2026-11-12 08:49 UTC · <a href="https://api.vultr.com/v2/plans">GET /v2/plans</a>. Backup multiplier: <a href="https://docs.vultr.com/support/platform/billing/how-much-does-it-cost-to-enable-automatic-backups">B, official documentation, opening body paragraph</a>.</p>\n<p>These are selected <code>vc2</code> records from the retrieved response, not the entire catalog. Bandwidth is the plan field in GB; it is not a statement of the account&#x27;s combined allowance or a guarantee of transfer available for a partial billing period. Unit definitions: <a href="https://docs.vultr.com/reference/terraform/data-sources/plan">Attributes Reference, bandwidth and monthly_cost</a>.</p>\n<h2>Regional prices: replacement price, not an extra fee</h2>\n<p>The table reproduces numeric <code>location_cost</code> records for the selected plans. Region codes are kept exactly as returned. A regional price is shown in its own column; the calculated difference is not another charge to add to that regional price.</p>\n<div class="table-wrap"><table>\n<tr><th>Plan / region</th><th>Default USD: month / hour</th><th>Regional USD: month / hour</th><th>Monthly difference, estimate</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>vc2-1c-1gb</code> / <code>sao</code> [P2.location_cost.sao]</td><td>$5.00 / $0.007 [P2.monthly_cost / hourly_cost]</td><td>$7.50 / $0.01 [P2.location_cost.sao.monthly_cost / hourly_cost]</td><td>$2.50, estimate [regional monthly − default monthly]</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>vc2-1c-2gb</code> / <code>sao</code> [P3.location_cost.sao]</td><td>$10.00 / $0.014 [P3.monthly_cost / hourly_cost]</td><td>$15.00 / $0.021 [P3.location_cost.sao.monthly_cost / hourly_cost]</td><td>$5.00, estimate [regional monthly − default monthly]</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>数据取自 Vultr 官方接口 · 2026-11-12 08:49 UTC · <a href="https://api.vultr.com/v2/plans">GET /v2/plans</a>; differences are calculated from the cited fields.</p>\n<p>An empty <code>location_cost</code> object does not establish a zero charge, regional availability or an N/A billing rule. No regional price is invented from an empty object. The <code>locations</code> list is catalog metadata, not a live stock check.</p>\n<h2>Automatic Backups: the source sentence and the calculation</h2>\n<p>Vultr&#x27;s <strong>How Much Does It Cost to Enable Automatic Backups?</strong>, opening body paragraph, states:</p>\n<blockquote>Enabling Automatic Backups on a Vultr instance incurs an additional 20% charge based on the instance’s base hourly or monthly price.</blockquote>\n<p><a href="https://docs.vultr.com/support/platform/billing/how-much-does-it-cost-to-enable-automatic-backups">B: Vultr backup-cost documentation, opening body paragraph</a>. The next body paragraph limits the charge to eligible instances with the feature enabled; the following paragraph says backup fees are prorated by instance uptime.</p>\n<p><strong>Calculated estimates for <code>vc2-1c-1gb</code>, using the listed monthly bases:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Default backup addition: $5.00 [P2.monthly_cost] × 20% [B] = <strong>$1.00/month, estimate</strong>.</li>\n<li>Default base plus backup: $5.00 + $1.00 = <strong>$6.00/month, estimate</strong> [preceding formula].</li>\n<li><code>sao</code> backup addition: $7.50 [P2.location_cost.sao.monthly_cost] × 20% [B] = <strong>$1.50/month, estimate</strong>.</li>\n<li><code>sao</code> base plus backup: $7.50 + $1.50 = <strong>$9.00/month, estimate</strong> [preceding formula].</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These estimates cover only the listed base and the documented backup percentage. They do not estimate an entire invoice or imply that unlisted costs are zero.</p>\n<h2>Audit check: keep hourly and monthly calculations separate</h2>\n<p>Do not reconstruct a listed hourly price by dividing a monthly price. For <code>vc2-1c-2gb</code>, the API independently returns <strong>$10.00/month</strong> [P3.monthly_cost] and <strong>$0.014/hour</strong> [P3.hourly_cost]. For an eligible instance, applying the documented backup percentage to that hourly base gives $0.014 × 20% = <strong>$0.0028/hour estimated backup addition</strong>, and $0.014 + $0.0028 = <strong>$0.0168/hour estimated base plus backup</strong> [P3.hourly_cost and B]. This calculation is not a separately quoted Vultr rate or a prediction of invoice rounding.</p>\n<h2>Field-level sources and freshness</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href="https://api.vultr.com/v2/plans">P1, P2, P3: Vultr public plans API</a>. Select the element of <code>plans[]</code> whose <code>id</code> equals, respectively, <code>vc2-1c-0.5gb</code>, <code>vc2-1c-1gb</code>, or <code>vc2-1c-2gb</code>. A label such as P2.location_cost.sao.monthly_cost means that exact property of the selected record; it does not mean array position.</li>\n<li><a href="https://docs.vultr.com/support/platform/billing/how-much-does-it-cost-to-enable-automatic-backups">B: Automatic Backup Costs</a>, opening body paragraph: backup percentage; subsequent body paragraphs: eligibility and proration.</li>\n<li><a href="https://docs.vultr.com/reference/terraform/data-sources/plan">Field units: vultr_plan, Attributes Reference</a>: <code>bandwidth</code> is GB and <code>monthly_cost</code> is USD per month.</li>\n<li>API retrieval: <strong>2026-11-12 08:49 UTC</strong>. The saved response, rather than any third-party table, is the input for every displayed plan figure. Prices and catalog entries may change after retrieval.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>No fields are labelled N/A. Unverified billing details are omitted rather than treated as inapplicable.</p><p><a href="./sources.json">Download the timestamped source records</a></p></main><footer>VPS Cost Lens · Independent price research</footer></body></html>'

